# S-044: per-tick sequence: active mask, buffers cleared before the input callback, callback fills them, active mixes
# are clamped (NaN -> 0, +-1 limits) with an unclamped copy, outputs are delivered with the callback-chosen timestamp.
aopen main 48000 FLOAT_PLANAR STEREO
# no inputs: callback still runs with mask 0 and every mix pointer table populated
atick
aconnect a 1 0
aconnect b 2 3
afeed 0 0 0 4 0.25 set
afeed 3 0 0 2 -3 set
afeed 3 1 0 1 nan set
afeed 3 1 1 1 inf set
afeed 3 1 2 1 -inf set
anewts delta 0
# mixes 0 and 3 active (mask 0x09); mix 3 is clamped: -3 -> -1, nan -> 0, +-inf -> +-1
aprobe 0 1 2 3 1023
atick
# buffers are cleared every tick: 'add' mode shows a fresh zero start each time
afeed_clear
afeed 0 0 0 1 0.5 add
atick 2
adump
aclose
